body: "## Evidenced SDK-upgrade test blocker\n[PR #187](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/pull/187), head `8eca1c4f16bbc00308dfd98fff2f853902ff5b70`, is tested as merge `5e639ab80fcd6bab319d58b1286315ef753655b7` into main `be4e877b1deb4150d1d195f2825ee77e0bb975a0`, with SDK `2026.11.1`. Head and failed checks reverified November4 at14:04 UTC.\n\n[Node22 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/actions/runs/41828727080/job/126570074635) and [Node26 job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/actions/runs/41828727080/job/126570073852) both report217 tests,209 passed,8 failed. All eight paginated-consumer tests fail during [fixture creation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/blob/8eca1c4f16bbc00308dfd98fff2f853902ff5b70/test/paginated-consumer.test.ts#L43-L47), before their intended assertions:\n`--parent must not use placeholder token \"none\". Use --unset parent to clear this field.`\n\nThe fixture passes `\"none\"` for parent, goal, objective, sprint, release and assignee.\n\n## Goal, expected and actual\nThe [canonical consumer acceptance criteria](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/blob/be4e877b1deb4150d1d195f2825ee77e0bb975a0/.agents/pm/features/pm-starter-cancellation-consumer.toon) require cancellation/resume and snapshot behavior against genuine native SDK reads with passing CI gates.\n\nExpected: valid native fixture items let those assertions execute. Actual: rejected fixture input blocks the SDK upgrade and full gate. This is a test-fixture migration defect; the evidence does not establish a consumer-runtime defect.\n\n[Core #1658](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1658) changes typed refusal wording and adds null clears, but still rejects `parent:\"none\"`; that PR alone does not migrate this caller.\n\n## Acceptance and regression criteria\n- Replace intended empty fixture scopes with supported omission/unset semantics; check all six former sentinel fields.\n- All eight genuine-native consumer tests execute and pass.\n- Full Node22/26 gates pass on the repaired exact head without weakening assertions, coverage, or replacing native reads with mocks.\n\n## Evidence limits and deduplication\nCI logs and immutable source only; no local reproduction or replacement-fixture validation. Complete189-entry all-status issue/PR collection, PR187 conversation, and canonical tracker records checked; no matching current defect owner found. PR187 is the existing SDK dependency-upgrade vehicle; this issue records its newly diagnosed fixture blocker, not a request for a second upgrade PR.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-04T23:38:59Z)\n>\n> Fixed by #187 (merged as b3e7b72): the pm-toolchain bump to pm-cli 2026.11.4 now clears typed fields with `unset` instead of placeholder sentinels (pm-cli GH-1614), its tests pass and its coverage meets the unchanged thresholds. The agent's commits were reviewed by a read-only codex reviewer before the merge."
